1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:12,060
Slide 3 exposes "THE ACTIVE TAB TRAP." James, describe what you see when developers try to run complex AI workflows in a browser.

2
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,602
It is pure comedy, Professor!

3
00:00:14,602 --> 00:00:23,780
I've literally seen junior developers leave their MacBook lids propped open with a coffee mug overnight just to keep Chrome from sleeping while their script runs!

4
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,880
Haha!

5
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:38,220
And the moment their home Wi-Fi blinks for two seconds, or their laptop battery dips, the WebSocket disconnects, the tab crashes, and five hours of multi-step data synthesis is completely wiped out!

6
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,320
Exactly!

7
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:46,951
Look at the left card: when you run an agent in a browser tab, your machine is a hostage.

8
00:00:46,951 --> 00:00:50,520
If you refresh the tab, your in-memory context vanishes!

9
00:00:51,420 --> 00:01:00,630
But look at the right card: "SPARK PERSISTENCE." The entire execution runtime lives inside an isolated Docker cloud container on Google Cloud.

10
00:01:00,630 --> 00:01:07,960
You shut your laptop, jump on an airplane, and the agent continues executing in the cloud without missing a beat!

11
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:11,440
And if the cloud container restarts?

12
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,640
No problem!

13
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:19,110
It reads the last checkpoint from SQLite and resumes right where it left off in 10 milliseconds!

14
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:26,830
Decoupling execution from your local browser is the foundational law of professional agentic IT.

